{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And you shall see it, and you shall be gathered to your people, you too.</b> Why was it necessary to repeat וראיתה אותה — was not וראה את הארץ already mentioned? Rather, וראיתה אותה means depicted on high, at the time you are gathered to your people. And the addition of the ה in the word וראיתה perhaps comes to hint that the seeing is by the power of the ה, and furthermore that the supernal earth is the final ה of the Name, and it is the glory of HaShem that will gather him; therefore the י is added in the word עמיך. And so in every instance of עמיך said regarding Moses our master, peace be upon him, we find that they are written with a י, and they are: ונאספת אל עמיך, (Numbers 31:2) אחר תאסף אל עמיך, (Deuteronomy 32:50) ומות בהר אשר אתה עולה שמה והאסף אל עמיך."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:32.324665521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}